<title>SPAIN: Argentaria sees its euro cost at 5 bln ptas.</title>
<headline>Argentaria sees its euro cost at 5 bln ptas.</headline>
<dateline>SANTANDER, Spain 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish bank Argentaria's chairman Francisco Gonzalez on Monday estimated the cost to adapt the group to the euro at five billion pesetas.</p>
<p>Speaking at a colloquium on the euro,  Gonzalez did not give a figure for lost business, but said the euro would provide the sector with new business opportunities.</p>
<p>The five billion would be technical adaptations and, to a smaller degree, training of personnel, he said.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
